# the lens- and tilt-independent constraint (why no close station can reproduce ref 062)
  ref 062 shows the dome cap ABOVE the near face's attic cornice. With the current stack (apex 53.4, attic 38.3 at r 22.2) that needs
      D > 76.4 m  -- independent of lens, tilt, framing and azimuth.
  to show it from D = 45 m instead you would need the apex at 74.2 m (now 53.4) OR the attic top at 27.8 m (now 38.3)
  to show it from D = 50 m instead you would need the apex at 67.7 m (now 53.4) OR the attic top at 30.3 m (now 38.3)
  The podium/rostra radius does not enter this inequality at all.

